This is an important viva question.

| KNN | SVM |
|---|---|
| K-Nearest Neighbors | Support Vector Machine |
| Distance-based algorithm | Margin-based algorithm |
| Finds nearest data points | Finds an optimal separating hyperplane |
| Uses majority voting | Uses a learned decision boundary |
| No traditional training model | Learns a model during training |
| Sensitive to feature scaling | Also benefits from feature scaling |

**Easy way to remember:**

- KNN → Looks at nearby examples.
- SVM → Finds the best boundary between classes.

